":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T14:21:08-07:00","id":644621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/635149-do-you-want-to-playtest-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=644605#post644605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might have an opening on Monday's game. I'll let y'all know later today.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In that case, I'll take my chance and request to be considered too!<br /> <br /> I'm in CST so Mountain time would be fine 95% of the time, especially if you're planning to start at 6 PM your time. I'm completely fine with video chat over Hangouts and potentially having those recorded for a blog or w/e. I've been a 1e player and ST for like 5 years, and I have a little play experience with 2e. I think that makes me comfortable enough with the game that I have some cool ideas and know what buttons to push (IE, what systems and setting elements to bring in), but I'd still be able to see things with fresh eyes.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to highlight that I have a good deal of recent experience learning how to give useful feedback on other peoples' writing, and being able to identify and put into words when and why something is or isn't working in general. &quot;Taking notes and giving feedback&quot; is something I would legitimately consider myself to be very good at, and I think that will translate to playtesting an RPG system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/ma